+    On macOS, the ID is interpreted as a pointer to an ``NSView``. Pass it as a
+    value cast to ``intptr_t``. mpv does not create a window of its own; instead
+    it inserts its render view as the bottom-most subview of the given view and
+    resizes it to track that view, so anything the host already placed there
+    composites on top of the video. Because the host owns the window,
+    ``--geometry``, ``--autofit*``, ``--fullscreen`` and the window state options
+    (``--ontop``, ``--window-maximized``, ``--window-minimized``, ``--border``)
+    have no effect, and mpv leaves the application activation policy, Dock icon
+    and menu bar alone.
